The selected asset should be visually highlighted.

Only one asset should be active at a time (unless multi-select is implemented in a future release).

2. Asset-Specific Migration Details

When an asset is selected, the entire Migration Planner should automatically update to display only the data for the selected asset.

Every panel, card, chart, recommendation, timeline, dependency graph, and migration analysis must refresh based on that specific asset.

Examples include:

Migration Readiness
Current Algorithms
Quantum Vulnerabilities
PQC Recommendations
Migration Timeline
Risk Analysis
Business Impact
Compatibility Analysis
Dependencies
Estimated Downtime
Rollback Strategy
Required Approvals
Success Probability
Compliance Impact

No information from other assets should appear while another asset is selected.

